# Cavity insert for an injection mould: a block with a filleted pocket for a lid, its walls
# offset for shrink, the floor moved up after a wall-thickness change, the top face put on the
# parting plane, a core pin deleted with its faces, a vent, ejector pins from a hole
# table, cooling channels across, a pry slot and chamfered edges.
pl = 36
shrink = 0.3
blk: extrude 40 rect -60 -40 120 80
cav: extrude cut 14 -xy at 0 0 40 rrect -40 -25 80 50 8
part: plane at 0 0 pl
replace (faces of blk normal +z) with part
# the floor up 1 for a thicker lid (TODO: after the fillet, as the change came, once regression move_face_by_blend holds)
move (faces of cav normal +z) by 0 0 1
fl: fillet 2 (edges of cav bottom)
offset -shrink (faces of cav) (faces of fl)
core: extrude 8 xy at 20 0 26 circle 0 0 4
# the cored hole in the lid dropped: its core pin goes, the floor healed
delete (faces of core)
vent: extrude cut 0.05 -xy at 0 0 pl rect 39 -3 21 6
pins: sketch xy
  pt -28 -14
  pt -28 14
  pt 0 -14
  pt 0 14
  pt 28 -14
  pt 28 14
end
ej: hole 4 on pins p1 thru
pattern ej pts pins
cool: hole 8 yz at -60 -30 12 thru
pattern cool lin 0 1 0 2 60
pry: extrude cut 3 -xy at -60 0 pl rect 0 -8 6 16
chamfer 2 (edges of blk along +z longer 30)
